# SentinelC

## Lightweight File Integrity Monitoring and Tamper Detection System in C

SentinelC is a lightweight file integrity monitoring and tamper detection prototype developed in C. It checks files against a previously created baseline and detects changes in monitored files.

## About the Project

The project was developed as part of the Structured Programming Language Sessional course in the Department of Cyber Security Engineering.

SentinelC creates a baseline of files in a selected folder. The baseline stores basic file information including the file name, file size, and FNV-1a 32-bit hash.

During an audit, SentinelC compares the current file information with the saved baseline and reports detected changes.

## Main Features

- Create a file baseline
- Calculate FNV-1a 32-bit hash
- Compare current files with the baseline
- Detect modified files
- Detect new files
- Detect deleted files
- Detect unchanged files
- Maintain an audit log
- Reset the existing baseline

## How It Works

The basic workflow is:

Baseline → File Size + Hash → Audit → Compare → Result → Audit Log

The system can report four main results:

- MATCH
- MODIFIED
- NEW FILE
- DELETED

