How to Run
Compile sentinel.c using a C compiler on Windows.
Run the generated executable.
Select Create Baseline.
Enter the folder path that you want to monitor.
Select Run Audit to compare the current files with the saved baseline.
Select View Audit Log to see recorded audit events.
Test Results

The project was tested using a sample folder containing text files.

The following cases were successfully tested:

MATCH: File remained unchanged.
MODIFIED: A change in an existing file was detected.
NEW FILE: A newly created file was detected.
DELETED: A deleted file was detected.
AUDIT LOG: Detected events were recorded in the audit log.
Limitations
The current version performs user-triggered audits rather than continuous real-time monitoring.
FNV-1a is used as a lightweight change-detection hash and is not a cryptographic hash such as SHA-256.
The project is a prototype for learning and academic purposes.
